# Docker-in-container workflow

All project tooling (package install, tests, lint, format, framework CLI) runs **inside containers**, not on the host.

## Pattern

1. Ensure the stack is up: `docker compose ps -q laravel.test`
2. Run commands via `docker compose exec laravel.test <command>`
3. Prefer documented `docker compose exec` forms from README when available.

```bash
docker compose exec laravel.test php artisan test
docker compose exec laravel.test composer install
docker compose exec laravel.test npm install
docker compose exec laravel.test vendor/bin/pint
```

## Forbidden on the host

- `php artisan …`
- `composer …`
- `phpunit` / `./vendor/bin/phpunit`
- `vendor/bin/pint`
- bare `npm test` / project tooling that depends on container PHP or DB

## Rationale

Runtime (PHP version, extensions, DB, queue) is defined by the container. Host invocations fail, or worse, silently use the wrong toolchain.
